# Sygg, Wanderwine Wisdom. Turn 1: Sygg is cast with the two moxes (its enter trigger targets itself). Turn 3: "at the
# beginning of your first main phase, you may pay {W}. If you do, transform Sygg" - the Plains pays as the ability
# resolves and Sygg turns over (CR 701.27a); "whenever this creature transforms into Sygg, Wanderbrine Shield, target
# creature you control gains protection from each color until your next turn" gives Sygg protection from all five colors,
# which is gone when turn 5 begins (CR 611.2b). Turn 5: paying {U} turns it back, and "whenever this creature enters or
# transforms into Sygg, Wanderwine Wisdom" (CR 701.27e) grants the target - Sygg - "whenever this creature deals combat
# damage to a player or planeswalker, draw a card" until end of turn. Sygg can't be blocked, so Bot2's Ornithopter does not
# stop it, and the damage draws Bot1 one card.

